# UI ownership

Before adding or changing UI (CSS, JS, HTML):

1. Read **`docs/architecture/ui/where-to-change-ui.md`** and search for existing classes, `aria-label`s, and helpers.
2. **Shared** look/behavior → `core-ui/assets/css/template-contract/` and `core-ui/assets/js/template/`.
3. **One route/page** → `portal/static/assets/css/route-overrides/` or `portal/static/assets/js/route-*`.
4. **Table column layout** → only `core-ui/.../template-table-profiles.css` (by `table[aria-label]`). Do not duplicate in `template-support-records.css` or route-overrides.
5. **Support inbox UI** (threads, badges, reply actions) → `template-support-records.css`, scoped to `table[aria-label="Support requests"]`.
6. Extend contract tests in `portal/tests/unit/css/` when adding table profiles or moving CSS across tiers.

Do not copy selector blocks to “make cascade work” — fix specificity or scoping instead (`:where()` utilities, scoped selectors).
